 Q-2
Hand-encode two Hack assembly programs to binary using the A-

instruction and C-instruction formats. Show the comp/dest/jump field

breakdowns.





Field Encoding Reference Key
a + comp (a c1c2c3c4c5c6):
D $\rightarrow$ 0 001100
M (a=1) $\rightarrow$ 1 110000
D+M (a=1) $\rightarrow$ 1 000010
D-M (a=1) $\rightarrow$ 1 010011
0 $\rightarrow$ 0 101010
dest (d1 d2 d3 = A D M):
null $\rightarrow$ 000 | M $\rightarrow$ 001 | D $\rightarrow$ 010
jump (j1 j2 j3 = < = >):
null $\rightarrow$ 000 | JGT (> 0) $\rightarrow$ 001 | JMP (unconditional) $\rightarrow$ 111
Program 1: Addition (Add.asm — Computes RAM[2] = RAM[0] + RAM[1])
Assembly Source & Symbol Resolution
Predefined symbols R0, R1, and R2 resolve to 0, 1, and 2, while (END) resolves to ROM address 6.
ROM Addr	Assembly Instruction	Resolved Instruction	Type
0	@R0	@0	A
1	D=M	D=M	C
2	@R1	@1	A
3	D=D+M	D=D+M	C
4	@R2	@2	A
5	M=D	M=D	C
6	(END) $\rightarrow$ @END	@6	A
7	0;JMP	0;JMP	C
